WEBVTT

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:14.300
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
aoku nemuru mizu no hoshi ni sotto

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
Kissing softly the star of water that sleeps in blue,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
kuchizuke shite inochi no hi wo tomosu hito yo

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
A person who lights the fire of life,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
toki to iu kin'iro no sazanami wa

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
The time, the golden ripple,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
oozora no kuchibiru ni umareta toiki ne

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
is a sigh from the lips of the sky,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
kokoro ni uzumoreta

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
The stars of kindness...

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
yasashisa no hoshitachi ga

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
...buried in heart flame up...

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
honoo age yobiau

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
...and call to each other,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
namima sasurau nanpasen no you ni

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
Like wrecked ships wandering on the waves...

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
mou nakanaide ima

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
Don't cry, any more,

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
anata wo sagashite iru hito ga iru kara

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
because now there is a person looking for you,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
omae ni aitai yo to

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
Dying to see you...

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:38.030
Char's actions during the meeting with
Haman Karn and the survivors of Zeon...

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.230
...led to a disastrous end
to their negotiations.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:47.070
As a result, Haman Karn formed ties
with Paptimus Scirocco instead.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:53.100
The Call of Darkness

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:11.000
We forwarded parts and spare
mobile suits to the Argama.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:13.130
Thank you, Lieutenant Emma.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.440
That should improve the position
of the Argama.

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:19.940
But only temporarily.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.940
The top concern is the crew's level
of fatigue.

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.270
They should give up trying to chase
the Gwadan...

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:27.320
...and plan to put the ship into dock.

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:30.280
Make sure you don't work
too hard either, Captain.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:34.790
You don't want to be too tired
for a date on your day off.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.020
Excuse me.

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:43.970
Here I go! One, two...!

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:47.260
What's going on?!

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:49.640
- Somebody!
- Help!

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.370
Shinta! Qum!

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:53.830
Help me!

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.210
- Kamille!
- Hold on tight.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.440
We were only trying to help.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:00.810
To help.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:03.040
I know.

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:06.080
Be extra careful here!

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.260
How is the Hyaku Shiki looking?

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:11.520
We've repaired it so it works - barely.

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:15.160
Lieutenant Quattro? You think he's okay?

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:17.460
He's a grown man.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.660
I'm sure he's got nothing to do with
the Principality of Zeon.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.640
Sure, I believe that too, but...!

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:24.230
The Zeta can hardly move either.

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:25.830
That's okay, as long as it moves.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:30.070
Well, you seem to have a much better
understanding of actual battle now.

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:33.210
How worthwhile it was
to "correct" you!

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:34.680
Thank you.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:36.310
What is it with that guy?!

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:38.050
He's just a very quarrelsome person!

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.990
Over there! What are you
slacking for?!

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:43.080
At your rate, we'll never defeat the Gwadan!

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:45.290
Lieutenant!

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:47.760
Are things okay with Ensign Reccoa?

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:49.020
What do you mean?

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:52.190
Fa told me you haven't visited
Miss Reccoa since she was hospitalized.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.870
I'll visit when I find the time.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:57.210
- There he goes again.
- What?

00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:01.840
Ensign Reccoa has a thing for
the lieutenant, yet he's always like that.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:05.240
There's nothing funny about it!

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:07.150
It's you that I find funny!

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:08.050
Why?!

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:11.420
Isn't it funny that you,
of all people, are talking in this way?

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:14.520
Do I seem like that much
of a geek to you?

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:17.690
Sure you do!

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:20.420
You really did fall in love
on Earth, didn't you?

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:23.460
Shinta! Qum!

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.030
I told you not to be here!

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:27.760
We were ordered to help!

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.830
- Don't lie to me!
- It's true!

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.100
Yeah, it's true.

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.770
These two are much more
welcome than that one.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.740
Why are you so slow?!
I thought you were professionals!

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:40.820
Isn't it a good thing
to be energetic?

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.110
By the way...

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:46.950
- ...I have a favor to ask you.
- S-Sure.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.520
Who is it?

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:52.890
- It's me.
- Come in.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:54.860
Miss Reccoa.

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:56.720
Should you be moving about like that?

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.930
I'm okay aside from some pain
in my right arm.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.260
But aren't you too busy to
visit me right now?

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:04.570
Kamille asked me to come
and see how you're doing.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:06.510
Kamille did?

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:07.540
Oh.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:11.480
Thank you, Fa, for taking the time
to come and see me.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:12.980
N-No problem.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.020
Fa...?

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:16.950
You're safe.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:33.470
I was so sure the doctor spotted
me from down the hallway.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.800
You enjoy this sort of thing,
don't you, Miss Reccoa?

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:38.330
Did Kamille say so?

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:43.810
I always get myself
into dangerous situations.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:45.950
It's now become a habit.

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:50.710
At one point, I used to live on the Moon.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:57.990
But I got separated from my parents
during the previous war.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:03.800
After that...

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:09.070
...I got involved in guerrilla activities,
and before I knew it, many friends died.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:27.990
I entered the Federation Forces
when the war ended.

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.320
But something was different.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:33.360
And before long,
I ended up with the A.E.U.G..

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:40.860
It wasn't through ideology or belief.

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:48.870
I don't get the sense that I'm alive
unless I live on the edge.

00:06:50.680 --> 00:06:52.880
That's become part of my personality.

00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:59.280
Also because the right man
never came along.

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:02.220
The right man?

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:05.390
Yes, the right man.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:08.630
From the beginning,
this world has had only two sexes.

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.330
Man and woman.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:14.090
In that case, there must be a meaning
for it, don't you think?

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:16.570
You're right.

00:07:17.770 --> 00:07:19.400
That makes sense.

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:26.080
You mustn't become a woman like me, Fa.

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:27.120
Sure.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:30.580
A-Although I'm not quite sure
what you mean.

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:32.010
You'll soon understand.

00:07:32.090 --> 00:07:34.390
I guess so. Bye.

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:43.130
This room isn't waiting for anyone
to be back here.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.640
The Gwadan's quietly following us.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:53.440
What do you have in mind, Scirocco?

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:58.310
It hasn't been this quiet for a long time.

00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:01.480
It's only quiet because
the Argama's not coming after us!

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:04.910
Let's hope nothing will happen.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.560
Stop stalling!

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:10.280
Don't you want to
destroy the Argama?!

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:12.520
Of course I do!

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:16.290
However, our priority at the moment
is to have the people on that ship...

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:18.330
...form an alliance with the Titans.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:21.700
Then don't we need to get rid of
any obstacles in our way?!

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:25.470
That would also make sense.

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:28.170
All right, do as you wish.

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:30.640
Scirocco.

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:33.850
You are necessary to me.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.840
With your help...

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:38.280
...I can bring the Titans and Axis together.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:40.520
I see.

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:43.460
So, can I assume that I'll be rewarded
for my actions?

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:46.420
Of course, Yazan.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:48.860
I like your personality.

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:51.320
Understood.

00:08:57.310 --> 00:08:58.400
Wait, Sarah!

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:00.970
There's no place for you in Yazan's warfare.

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:05.240
Just observe, understanding his tactics
is yet another way to battle.

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:07.670
You understand, right?

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:28.900
Why isn't the captain on the bridge now...

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:31.440
...while we're pursuing the enemy?!

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:33.370
He's here.

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:35.200
Mr. Wong?

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:36.570
Where the hell were you?!

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:40.350
I was helping with the repairs
to the hull.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:43.280
That's not a job for the captain!

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:46.540
In any case, I find this ship
to lack order and discipline!

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:47.850
Mr. Wong.

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.720
Don't you think
that's one of the main reasons...

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:52.850
...the Argama's been able to
survive battles to this point?

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:56.560
Then why did we fail
in our negotiation with Axis?!

00:09:57.600 --> 00:09:59.730
I was against it in the first place.

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:02.230
When are we going to catch up
with the enemy?

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:04.570
We're docking at La Vie En Rose first.

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:07.400
You're going to waste precious time
while docked.

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:10.240
The Radish's backup only allows us
to do temporary repairs.

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:13.240
Should the enemy attack us
with a large force, we don't stand a chance!

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:17.580
In war, it's very rare to
be able to fight in top condition!

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:19.780
As Lieutenant Quattro was saying...

00:10:19.860 --> 00:10:22.820
...I thought the Argama could make
even "the impossible" possible!

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:25.260
Not in this state!

00:10:26.630 --> 00:10:28.760
Captain! Enemy mobile suit team detected!

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:29.830
What?!

00:10:30.070 --> 00:10:32.970
- How many?!
- Six, as far as I can confirm.

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:34.560
Six...!

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:36.570
- Send out our mobile suits!
- Roger!

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:42.580
What is it?

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:45.270
I thought I just heard something.

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:52.090
Kamille.

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:54.090
Is the Zeta Gundam ready to go?!

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:55.620
I'll take the launcher with me.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:03.790
What are you doing, Ensign Reccoa?!

00:11:08.170 --> 00:11:10.200
Ensign Reccoa!
You're in no condition to go!

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:12.640
You'd better return to your room.

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:15.280
I am a pilot on the Argama!

00:11:16.010 --> 00:11:16.980
Reccoa.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.950
What's gotten into you, Reccoa Londe?!

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:22.810
Have you...

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:28.380
...have you done anything to convince me
not to go?!

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:31.730
Ensign.

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:39.830
What do you...

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:42.530
...want me to do?

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:21.070
We've brought out all of them, have we?

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:22.300
<i>We're done!</i>

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.210
Okay, I want just two of you
to stay here.

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:26.340
Keep them moving so
the enemy doesn't catch on.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.410
Zeta Gundam, taking off!

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:35.820
Mk. II, taking off!

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:39.890
The pain just won't go away.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:42.320
Methuss, taking off!

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:48.900
How beautiful.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:55.200
The Methuss?!

00:12:55.280 --> 00:12:56.540
Is Ensign Reccoa out here?

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:02.310
<i>Ensign Reccoa, you're out too far!</i>

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:04.910
- <i>Move back!</i>
- Kamille?

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:07.150
Are you the one who's been calling me?

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:09.050
No.

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:11.090
Miss Reccoa! Move away!

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:15.630
Okay, spread out!

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.360
Be careful!

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:20.400
<i>Roger!</i>

00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:39.880
It's the Zeta.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.620
Watch out for the launcher!

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:54.700
Let go!

00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:57.470
<i>I can hear it.</i>

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:00.000
<i>A very powerful will.</i>

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:04.080
Got you!

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:10.490
Reccoa!

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:12.550
Ramsus! Don't bother! Let it go!

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:13.520
Roger!

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:17.090
Reccoa!

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.750
Charging with the Methuss alone?!

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:24.430
It escaped?!

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:26.970
Enemy mobile suits
aren't able to get any closer!

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:28.900
Way to go!

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:32.340
Tell Lieutenant Quattro and Kamille
to scout the rear of the enemies!

00:14:38.150 --> 00:14:40.310
<i>I thought it was peculiar as well.</i>

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:43.320
Are they waiting for us to lower
our guard before they attack?

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:45.480
We'd better check it out!

00:14:46.420 --> 00:14:47.550
Ensign Reccoa!

00:14:51.730 --> 00:14:53.020
<i>Miss Reccoa!</i>

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:55.890
Why am I... all the way out here?

00:14:56.530 --> 00:14:58.020
You're out too far!

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:00.030
What's the matter?!

00:15:00.270 --> 00:15:01.240
Sorry!

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:03.030
<i>It's not like you, Ensign Reccoa!</i>

00:15:03.510 --> 00:15:04.340
Lieutenant Quattro.

00:15:05.210 --> 00:15:06.070
I'm going!

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:08.440
<i>Kamille! Thank you for that.</i>

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:10.670
Miss Reccoa.

00:15:12.610 --> 00:15:13.580
What is wrong with her?

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:25.060
They're here!

00:15:27.900 --> 00:15:28.860
What?!

00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:30.400
Why those are...!

00:15:37.340 --> 00:15:39.900
Marasais. There's at least ten!

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:41.540
Kamille, contact the Radish!

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:43.170
I'll contact the Argama!

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:46.440
That's right! There's a Marasai squadron
ahead of us!

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:48.480
Lt. Emma, head over there right away!

00:15:48.820 --> 00:15:50.250
What do you plan to do?!

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:52.410
Prepare to fire the Mega Particle Cannon!

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:53.250
Ensign Reccoa!

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:54.720
Answer me, Ensign!

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:56.760
What's wrong? Isn't she answering?

00:15:57.790 --> 00:15:59.620
Ensign Reccoa! Can't you hear me?!

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:00.820
Mr. Wong!

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.490
We're in a battle!

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:04.560
Stop walking around,
and remain in your seat!

00:16:05.470 --> 00:16:06.490
What did you say?!

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:09.990
I am the captain of this ship!

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:12.300
If you cannot abide by my orders,
I'll have you leave the ship!

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:13.670
Ensign Reccoa!

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:16.770
Ensign, fall back and protect the Argama
from the other mobile suits!

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:19.310
Roger!

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:21.910
I missed my chance again.

00:16:28.890 --> 00:16:30.860
They're playing right into our hands!

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:32.590
<i>Leader!</i>

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:33.490
Let's go!

00:16:36.770 --> 00:16:39.790
Two enemy mobile suits
have crossed the defensive line!

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:42.300
We'll retreat in a zigzag course
as we return fire!

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:43.770
Don't let them attack the Argama!

00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:48.040
Hurry!

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:51.240
We've got to crush the Argama before
they discover our ruse and return!

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:58.380
You're in my way! I'll start with you!

00:17:08.530 --> 00:17:10.000
You're in my way! Go away!

00:17:16.040 --> 00:17:17.200
That's my enemy?

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:19.810
<i>Kamille, let's do it!</i>

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:20.840
Roger!

00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:22.640
What was that?

00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:25.410
Let's go!

00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:30.880
They're not real! They're dummies!

00:17:30.950 --> 00:17:32.390
Bridge, come in!

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:34.390
It's from Lieutenant Emma!

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:36.550
She says the Marasais are all fake.

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:37.020
What?!

00:17:37.090 --> 00:17:39.560
Enemy mobile suits approaching
the Argama!

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:41.850
We've been tricked!

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:44.230
Call back the mobile suits!

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:51.730
Why can't I fire?!

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:56.850
Die!

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:02.780
I can't move. Why?!

00:18:03.650 --> 00:18:05.350
Wh-What is this?

00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:07.450
Why won't it move? Is it a dummy?

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:15.060
I won't be tricked by an illusion!

00:18:19.940 --> 00:18:21.230
Is it the power of this person...

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:24.000
...that was calling me?

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:28.880
Wh-What is it with this guy?!

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:44.280
I'm going to die. Yet, I'm not one bit scared.

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:46.950
Right. That's why I wanted to die.

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:52.270
But if someone's out there
calling for me, then...

00:18:52.430 --> 00:18:53.870
Who is it?!

00:18:53.940 --> 00:18:55.840
You? Is it you?!

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:58.510
Why'd it come? What?!

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:05.340
Tell me! Was it you that called me?!

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:14.320
<i>Leader!</i>

00:19:14.390 --> 00:19:16.620
<i>They've found out that</i>
<i>they're balloons!</i>

00:19:16.690 --> 00:19:18.820
<i>The Argama's mobile suit team</i>
<i>is heading back there!</i>

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:21.430
I hear you! Roger!

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:23.020
We're pulling back, Ramsus!

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:40.510
Is it this man? This...?

00:19:42.080 --> 00:19:44.520
She seems like a decent woman.

00:19:44.590 --> 00:19:45.990
Why?

00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:01.600
Kamille.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.170
What's wrong?

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:05.900
Ensign Reccoa...

00:20:06.170 --> 00:20:07.700
Miss Reccoa...!

00:20:10.150 --> 00:20:11.110
Fa!

00:20:11.950 --> 00:20:14.070
Miss Reccoa's dead!

00:20:15.350 --> 00:20:17.340
Wh-What are you saying?

00:20:18.450 --> 00:20:20.320
Stop joking.

00:20:20.390 --> 00:20:23.550
How could I joke about
something like this?!

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:25.430
That can't be.

00:20:25.490 --> 00:20:27.620
The Methuss exploded.

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:31.360
If I hadn't helped her sneak out
of the infirmary...!

00:20:33.270 --> 00:20:35.130
It's not your fault, Fa.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:37.190
Don't blame yourself!

00:20:37.610 --> 00:20:38.540
Miss Reccoa...

00:20:38.610 --> 00:20:40.840
...went out on her own will.

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:46.980
Kamille.

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:51.980
Do you realize the unstable condition
the crew is in at the moment?

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:55.050
But the Argama has coped with
harder situations, hasn't it?

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:58.120
I'm not talking only from
a material point of view...

00:20:58.190 --> 00:20:59.420
...but about their mental state as well!

00:20:59.490 --> 00:21:01.330
I'm also well aware of that!

00:21:02.300 --> 00:21:06.530
Many are very disturbed right now, having
one of our regular pilots killed in action.

00:21:06.600 --> 00:21:09.000
Then, at least our outfit needs
to be fully equipped.

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:13.570
I also ask the same, Mr. Wong Lee.

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:16.510
Never mind me and do as you wish!

00:21:16.650 --> 00:21:18.980
Do you believe that is the correct way
to do things?!

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:21.050
Of course.

00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:23.910
When it comes to battles,
you guys are the pros.

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:26.980
We should reach the dock ship,
the La Vie En Rose shortly.

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:28.150
Get in touch with them.

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:40.030
I looked for you, Lieutenant Quattro.

00:21:45.810 --> 00:21:49.370
If you had been just a little more kind
to Miss Reccoa...

00:21:49.440 --> 00:21:51.410
...this wouldn't have happened!

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:53.450
Do you realize that?!

00:21:56.950 --> 00:22:00.950
Right now, Miss Reccoa is likely
floating in the dark of space...!

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:10.090
The cactus flowers have blossomed.

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:26.270
In their battle against Yazan,
the Argama and the Radish...

00:22:26.350 --> 00:22:28.320
...were dealt a severe blow.

00:22:29.020 --> 00:22:32.780
However, at the La Vie En Rose,
where they are docked for repairs...

00:22:32.850 --> 00:22:35.820
...they are about to be given a new order.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:47.930 --> 00:23:49.690
After eluding an attack by the Yazan team...

00:23:49.760 --> 00:23:53.860
...the Hyaku Shiki descends
to Kilimanjaro with the Zeta Gundam.

00:23:54.740 --> 00:23:58.900
Upon sneaking into the Titans' base,
Char and Kamille see Jamitov...

00:23:58.970 --> 00:24:00.370
...and Four.

00:24:01.510 --> 00:24:06.040
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Storm Over Kilimanjaro".

00:24:06.780 --> 00:24:09.450
You will see the tears of time.

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Next Episode

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Storm Over Kilimanjaro
